From: ArchR <noreply@arch-r.io>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtl8xxxu: ratelimit the unhandled C2H dump

rtl8723bu_handle_c2h() runs for every RX report, from the USB
completion's softirq, and printed each unknown event with a hex dump of
its whole length. A dongle delivering garbage descriptors (an R36S
Soysauce's RTL8723BU, 2026-11-21) turned that into a printk flood that
held CPU0 for 45 s: "soft lockup - CPU#0 stuck for 45s!
[irq/26-dwc2_hso]" in vprintk_store from rtl8xxxu_parse_rxdesc24, then
a panic. Print it at most at the network ratelimit, 32 bytes at most.
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8xxxu/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8xxxu/core.c
@@ -6223,10 +6223,18 @@
 			c2h->ra_report.macid, c2h->ra_report.noisy_state);
 		break;
 	default:
-		dev_info(dev, "Unhandled C2H event %02x seq %02x\n",
-			 c2h->id, c2h->seq);
-		print_hex_dump(KERN_INFO, "C2H content: ", DUMP_PREFIX_NONE,
-			       16, 1, c2h->raw.payload, len, false);
+		/*
+		 * Runs for every RX report in the USB completion's softirq: a
+		 * dongle sending garbage descriptors turned this into a flood
+		 * that held the CPU for 45 s (a soft lockup panic).
+		 */
+		if (net_ratelimit()) {
+			dev_info(dev, "Unhandled C2H event %02x seq %02x\n",
+				 c2h->id, c2h->seq);
+			print_hex_dump(KERN_INFO, "C2H content: ",
+				       DUMP_PREFIX_NONE, 16, 1,
+				       c2h->raw.payload, clamp(len, 0, 32), false);
+		}
 		break;
 	}
 
